Compiled Linux device trees in tests/fixtures/io
================================================

The following test fixtures are binary (DTB) builds of BSD-3-Clause device
tree sources from Linux arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom, revision
40288c9206c17eb66a603262e06a58d300d0f279 (how each was built: README.md in
the fixture's directory):

  tests/fixtures/io/sm8650-qrd.dtb
  tests/fixtures/io/sm8650-ayaneo-pocket-s2.dtb   (plus the MIT RFC touch node
                                                   of sm8650-ayaneo-pocket-s2-rfc-touch.dts)
  tests/fixtures/io/qup/sm8250-hdk.dtb
  tests/fixtures/io/qup/sm8150-hdk.dtb
  tests/fixtures/io/goodix/sm8650-qrd.dtb
  tests/fixtures/io/goodix/sm8650-ayaneo-pocket-s2.dtb

Each blob has a REUSE-style "<file>.license" sidecar naming its licence.
The rest of kShimC is MIT (LICENSE at the top of the tree). The compiled
sources and their copyright notices:

  sm8650.dtsi, sm8650-qrd.dts               Copyright (c) 2023, Linaro Limited
  sm8650-ayaneo-pocket-s2.dts               Copyright (c) 2023, Linaro Limited
                                            Copyright (c) 2025, Kancy Joe <kancy2333@outlook.com>
  pm8010.dtsi, pm8550.dtsi, pm8550b.dtsi,
  pm8550ve.dtsi, pm8550vs.dtsi,
  pmk8550.dtsi, pmr735d_a.dtsi              Copyright (c) 2022, Linaro Limited
  sm8250.dtsi, sm8250-hdk.dts,
  sm8150-hdk.dts                            Copyright (c) 2020, The Linux Foundation. All rights reserved.
  sm8150.dtsi, pm8150.dtsi, pm8150b.dtsi,
  pm8150l.dtsi                              Copyright (c) 2017-2019, The Linux Foundation. All rights reserved.
                                            Copyright (c) 2019, Linaro Limited

The include/dt-bindings headers the preprocessor used contribute only
numeric constants (clock, reset, interrupt and GPIO IDs) to the blobs; no
header text is contained in them.

